\name{sdrf_pool}
\alias{sdrf_pool}
\title{Merge several SDRF documents into one analysis table}
\usage{
sdrf_pool(documents, out = NULL, limit = NULL, offset = 0, timeout = 60)
}
\arguments{
\item{documents}{A character vector of paths. \strong{Name it} to choose each document's provenance
  label: \code{c(malaria = "PXD000070.sdrf.tsv", colon = "PXD026824.sdrf.tsv")}. Name every element
  or none.}

\item{out}{Write the merged document here as SDRF. The \strong{whole} document is written regardless
  of \code{limit} and \code{offset}.}

\item{limit}{Maximum rows to return. \code{NULL}, the default, returns all of them.}

\item{offset}{Rows to skip.}

\item{timeout}{Seconds to allow, or \code{NULL} to wait indefinitely.
}

}
\description{
Columns are the union of every document's, ordered by SDRF's own block structure, and a name
that repeats is carried at the highest multiplicity any single document used, so nothing is
dropped. A cell a document did not have is filled with the reserved word \code{"not available"}, and
a \code{comment[source document]} column records which document each row came from.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_pooled_sdrf}, which is also an \code{mzlibr_sdrf}: everything \code{\link{sdrf_read}}
  returns, plus \code{document_count}, \code{paths}, \code{labels}, and \code{written} (a list of \code{path} and
  \code{row_count}, or \code{NULL} when \code{out} was not given).

}
\section{Give your documents names}{


With an unnamed vector, mzLib falls back to \code{containing-folder/file-stem}, which depends on
where the files happen to sit - so the same documents pooled from a different directory produce
a different table. The returned \code{caveats} say so when that fallback was used.

}
\section{The result is an analysis table, not something to deposit}{


Source name, assay name and label together are unique within one document, but two
experiments may both have a \code{"Sample 1"}, so a pooled table will usually violate SDRF's
uniqueness rule. Use \code{\link{sdrf_source_documents}} as part of any key.

}
